.nh
.TH "PB-SESSION-LIST" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-session-list - List terminal sessions on every machine, or on one


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb session list [machine] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List terminal sessions on every machine, or on one

.PP
Without a machine, list the sessions on every machine of the workspace (the same list on every computer); with one, only that machine's. Shows the automatic application title or foreground process and current directory where observed. “Started in” labels the launch directory when current metadata is unavailable. --wide adds the session ID; choose an exact session ID for attach, rename, close, or sharing.

.PP
Terminal sessions persist independently of a single connection and can be reattached after a disconnect. Sharing grants explicit access to a named session. Closing, deleting, and removing a participant have different effects; inspect the selected session before acting.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--all\fP[=false]
	show every item, up to 10000

.PP
\fB--closed\fP[=false]
	filter explicitly by closed state

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=50
	show at most this many items (1-200)

.PP
\fB--owner\fP=""
	filter owner: mine, shared, or an authorized account ID

.PP
\fB--q\fP=""
	filter by resource name or ID

.PP
\fB--state\fP=""
	filter by resource state

.PP
\fB--wide\fP[=false]
	include immutable IDs


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-session(1)\fP
